RNN-FFWD: fix for #10
https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/10

ffwd_sig() is given nodes_0+1 inputs, so the fed-back outputs never reach the nodes: the
"recurrent" network ran as a single tanh neuron. Feed all nodes_0+nodes_1+1 inputs, in training
and test. This is the bug the author always suspected; with it fixed and the learning rate
re-tuned the RNN beats the ADALINE on the telephone channel above 10 dB.

Applies to the sources prepared by src/tools/prepare.py (wrapped lines rejoined,
names lower-cased), not to src/borland/ directly:
  patch -p1 -d <prep dir> < src/fixes/RNN-FFWD.patch

--- a/rnn.c
+++ b/rnn.c
@@ -137,8 +137,9 @@
 
         /* Feed inputs through net */
 
+                                        /* Fix #10: the fed-back outputs never reached the nodes
+                                         * https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/10 */
-                                        ffwd_sig(ann.layer_0, ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_0+1,
-ann.nodes_1);
+                                        ffwd_sig(ann.layer_0, ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_0+ann.nodes_1+1, ann.nodes_1);
 
         /* Calculate error and store square error */
 
@@ -264,7 +265,9 @@
 
 /* Feed inputs through net */
 
+                                /* Fix #10: the fed-back outputs never reached the nodes
+                                 * https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/10 */
-                                ffwd_sig(ann.layer_0, ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_0+1, ann.nodes_1);
+                                ffwd_sig(ann.layer_0, ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_0+ann.nodes_1+1, ann.nodes_1);
 
 /* Calculate output of equalizer and then work out its error */
 
